  "project_description": "The Views Striping module adds CSS classes to a view's rows to create stripes of alternating colours.\n\n Two striping methods are provided:\n\n \n Striping alternates each row \n Striping switches when a particular column's value changes \n \n You will need to define CSS styling for the 'odd' and 'even' classes in your theme.\n\n This currently only works for the table view style and the aggregated views table style.\n\n Similar modules \n \n Views Parity Row allows switching the entity view mode for alternating rows",
